<!--
  a link that opens a screen of this app, set at the end of the link's own text.

  **it is the counterpart to `ic_open_link` and the pair is the point.** an arrow out of a box means a
  browser and this means a screen of this app, which is a distinction somebody can act on before
  pressing rather than after.

  **it is a drawable rather than the character U+203A, which is what stood here first.** that character
  is a single right-pointing angle *quotation mark*: punctuation, drawn at punctuation's size and
  sitting where punctuation sits, so it read as a stray quote rather than as a chevron. this is an
  arrowhead at the weight of the text it follows.

  the same shape `ic_expand` carries, turned a quarter. it is a file of its own rather than that one
  rotated, because a compound drawable cannot be rotated where it is placed, and a rotation wrapper
  around a vector is a second indirection to read through for one glyph.

  Material's `chevron_right`, at Material Symbols' 960 viewport, sized and tinted for the reasons
  `ic_open_link` states.

  **the box carries empty space above the glyph, and that is how it is aligned.** a compound drawable
  is centred on the text view's line box, whose centre sits above the text's own optical centre, so
  left alone the mark rides high. nothing at the point of use can move it, but a taller box does:
  adding E of space above the glyph keeps the box centred and therefore moves the glyph down by E/2.
  so the space above is twice the shift wanted, 3.4dp here, measured against the line this mark
  follows rather than guessed.

  **it scales with the text and is not a constant.** the shift comes out of the font's metrics, so a
  different text size wants it measured again rather than copied. `ratio.py` and `align.py` beside this
  project's notes are what measure it.
  **the box is trimmed to the glyph, which the arrow's already was.** `open_in_new` fills its viewport
  to within 120 units of each edge; a chevron drawn at Material's own scale leaves 320 on the left and
  344 on the right, so at the same drawable padding it sat further from its word and pushed whatever
  followed further away again. the viewport here is cut to leave the same 120 either side, so both
  marks keep the same distance from the text without either of them being told a different padding.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="6.14dp"
    android:height="14.4dp"
    android:viewportWidth="536"
    android:viewportHeight="1257">
    <group
        android:translateX="-200"
        android:translateY="297">
        <path
            android:fillColor="@android:color/white"
            android:pathData="M504,480L320,296L376,240L616,480L376,720L320,664L504,480Z" />
    </group>
</vector>
